Step 3 · A hosted writer and reviewer (OpenRouter)
  Native Sessions pay for OpenRouter with your OpenRouter credits, so Axocoatl can count what each call costs. BYOK ("bring your own key") is another provider's API key, such as OpenAI's or Anthropic's, added to your OpenRouter account at https://openrouter.ai/settings/integrations: OpenRouter then sends calls to that provider on your key and the provider bills you, so Axocoatl cannot count the cost, and native Sessions refuse it. A new OpenRouter account has no BYOK keys.
? Use OpenRouter credits, with no BYOK provider keys connected? (Native Sessions do not support BYOK) [Y/n]
  answered yes
? Model for the writer (vendor/model) → qwen/qwen3-coder-30b-a3b-instruct
? Model for the reviewer (must be a different model) → openai/gpt-oss-120b
? How should Axocoatl get your OpenRouter key? → Sign in to OpenRouter in your browser (recommended)
